title: Measure a remote usage store before building UsageStore::Buffered
updated: 2026-08-08T14:24:53Z
---

Measured: jsonlog costs nothing (karr #10). NOT measured: a DBI backend against a real PostgreSQL over TCP, which is a round-trip on the request path and can hang or fail.

Measure that first with bench/. Only if it costs real time, add a UsageStore::Buffered decorator around any store: bounded queue, flush on batch size or timer, flush on shutdown, JsonLog stays synchronous.

Overflow policy must be drop-and-count-loudly. Silently dropping billing data under a sink outage is the worst possible failure. Note the trade against ADR 0004: a crash loses one event today, up to N with buffering -- that is a config decision, not a default.

Separately and cheaply: when no usage store is configured at all, record_usage still builds the whole event before discovering there is no sink. Skip the work when disabled.
